WEBVTT

00:23:29.522 --> 00:23:32.407
that there's this value
conflict for people

00:23:32.431 --> 00:23:34.686
that does feel like moral distress

00:23:34.710 --> 00:23:36.726
as a driver of burnout.

00:23:36.750 --> 00:23:39.893
And that, for me,
is where the burnout story began.

00:23:40.900 --> 00:23:43.636
AG: So Adrienne set out to find a cure.

00:23:43.660 --> 00:23:46.603
Healthcare professionals
are among the few occupational groups

00:23:46.627 --> 00:23:49.526
whose emotional exhaustion rates
rival teachers'.

00:23:49.550 --> 00:23:52.606
Nearly half of physicians
report being burned out.

00:23:52.630 --> 00:23:57.546
That costs the US economy
about 4.6 billion dollars a year.

00:23:57.570 --> 00:23:59.296
When doctors and nurses burn out,

00:23:59.320 --> 00:24:02.666
they're prone to anxiety,
depression and self-harm.